From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: a duplicated frame says it has a dirty rectangle (TotalMetadataBufferSize)

2611's AcquireNextFrame left DXGI_OUTDUPL_FRAME_INFO's TotalMetadataBufferSize
at 0, although GetFrameDirtyRects then gives the whole output. On Windows it
is the size of the frame's move and dirty rectangles, and programs read the
rectangles -- and copy the picture -- only when it is not 0: TightVNC's
Desktop Duplication capture (UseD3D, its default) copied nothing and its
viewers saw black (i0633). It is now one RECT. sg-d3d's DXVK has the same
fix (sg-image dxvk/patches/0016).

Gate: test/dxgidup-gate.sh (the metadata size is one RECT). Mutant
SG_MUTANT_DUP_NO_METADATA.
---
--- a/dlls/dxgi/output_dup.c
+++ b/dlls/dxgi/output_dup.c
@@ -267,6 +267,12 @@
             QueryPerformanceCounter(&now);
             frame_info->LastPresentTime = now;
             frame_info->AccumulatedFrames = 1;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DUP_NO_METADATA
+            /* the bytes of the frame's move and dirty rectangles (9656):
+             * none moved, the whole output dirty. Programs read them, and
+             * copy the picture, only when this is not 0 (TightVNC) */
+            frame_info->TotalMetadataBufferSize = sizeof(RECT);
+#endif
             hr = ID3D11Texture2D_QueryInterface(dup->texture, &IID_IDXGIResource, (void **)resource);
             if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
                 dup->frame_held = TRUE;
